course: dictionary
lesson: 13899
title: On the lam
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words hide a secret meaning, and the words around them give the clues. «The thief escaped from the prison last night and has been on the lam ever since.» Escaped and prison are the clues. A thief who escaped from prison is running away and hiding, so on the lam means running away and hiding.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The police searched the woods, but the robber was still on the lam.» If on the lam means running away and hiding, the sentence makes sense. If you swapped in sitting in a cafe, it would not.
explain: Lam can also be a verb, so its ending can change: lams, lammed, lamming. In an old film, you might hear, «The bully said he would lam the boy who took his sweets.» Here lam means to hit someone hard. This meaning is old-fashioned and rare, so you will mostly meet on the lam.
explain: Lam is also a family name, as in Chinese and Vietnamese families. When lam is a name, it starts with a capital letter, like Mia Lam. Read the clues to decide which meaning is right.
fact: On the lam means running away and hiding, usually from the police.
fact: On the lam is slang, so you will often meet it in crime stories, detective books and old films.
fact: To lam someone (informal, UK) means to hit them hard, but this is old-fashioned and rare.
fact: Lam is also a family name, for example in Chinese and Vietnamese families.
fact: Lam can be a verb with the forms lams, lammed and lamming.
exercise: «The thief escaped from prison and has been on the lam for three days.» What does on the lam mean? | *Running away and hiding | Winning a prize | Sitting quietly in a park | Cooking a big dinner
exercise: A detective says, «The suspect is on the lam, so we must find him fast.» Where is the suspect? | On holiday by the sea | At the police station, helping with questions | In a school hall, singing | *Hiding from the police
exercise: In an old film, the bully says, «I will lam you!» What does lam mean here? | To hug someone warmly | *To hit someone hard | To sing loudly | To lock a door
test: Which meaning fits best in «The robber was still on the lam»? | Being very tall | *Running away and hiding | Reading a book by the fire
test: Which sentence uses lam as a family name? | The boy was on the lam from the police. | The robber stayed on the lam for a week. | The bully said he would lam the boy. | *Mia Lam came to our school today.
exam: Ella thinks lam means a lamp, like a light in a room. Why is she wrong? | *Here on the lam means running away and hiding, not a light | Lam means lots of light | Lamp is spelled the same as lam, so it must mean the same | Lam is a kind of food
